# Information Architecture — Smart Onboarding 

Home / Dashboard
Personalised overview of tasks, progress, and updates

├── Before Starting
│   ├── Welcome message and company overview
│   ├── Pre-arrival paperwork and setup (equipment, accounts)
│   └── What to expect on Day 1
│
├── Onboarding Tasks (ongoing — not just Day 1)
│   ├── Task checklist, prioritised and updated as onboarding progresses
│   ├── Progress tracker (Day 1 → First week → First month milestones)
│   └── Smart reminders for incomplete tasks (surfaces overdue or
│       upcoming tasks automatically, not just a static list)
│
├── Role-Based Learning
│   ├── Role overview and responsibilities
│   ├── Role-specific learning modules (replaces generic-only training)
│   ├── Mandatory training (compliance, still required but clearly
│       separated from role-specific content)
│   └── Quizzes and checkpoints
│
├── Information Hub
│   ├── Company policies and procedures
│   ├── Key documents, always showing latest version + last-updated date
│   └── Announcements and FAQs
│
├── Help and Support
│   ├── Team directory and key contacts
│   ├── Manager check-ins
│   ├── Buddy / mentor contact
│   └── Support suggestion feature — guides the user to the right
│       channel (HR, IT, or manager) based on the type of question,
│       rather than a flat contact list
│
└── AI / Smart Support
    ├── Ask-anything AI assistant
    ├── Answers always show source + last-updated date
    └── Automatically escalates to a human for HR, salary,
        disciplinary, or legal questions





## Traceability to hypotheses

| IA Section | Hypothesis |
|---|---|
| Onboarding Tasks | H1 — Guided first steps + progress |
| Information Hub | H2 — Centralised information / single source of truth |
| Help and Support, AI / Smart Support | H3 — Trustworthy, contextual support |
| Role-Based Learning | H4 — Role-specific content over generic training |
